 #:seon.task{:name "alias-and-require-as-retarget-silently"
  :intent "In SCI, (require '[clojure.set :as x]) after x -> clojure.string returns nil and retargets the alias; so does (alias 'x 'clojure.walk) (sci-alias is a bare assoc-in, namespaces.cljc:478-486). Clojure refuses a different target (Namespace.java:257-258, \"Alias x already exists in namespace .., aliasing ..\"). The silent retarget makes stored definitions position-dependent and is the source of the digest refusals in the alias design probes. Correct: alias and require :as with a different target refuse as Clojure does, ns-unalias! being the guarded path (SCI runs ns-unalias itself); a refer replacement stays legal (a warning in Clojure). Related issue docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md. Proof: evaluating (alias 'x 'clojure.set) after x -> clojure.string answers a refusal error and leaves the alias unchanged. Read `my.program/ns-unalias!`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/alias-design.md` and `docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md`."}
